### Device-specific replacement for the droid.pa that
### droid-configs-device/sparse ships.
###
### Our sparse/ tree is copied last (see copy_files_from in
### droid-configs.inc), so this file supersedes the common one. Same package
### owns both paths, so there is no rpm file conflict.
###
### The ONLY change from upstream is that module-droid-hidl is not loaded.
###
### WHY
###
### This device does not use module-droid-card at all - its audio HAL is
### 32-bit and PulseAudio is 64-bit, so audio goes through plain ALSA instead.
### See /etc/pulse/arm_droid_card_custom.pa for the full explanation.
###
### module-droid-hidl needs module-droid-card to have loaded a hw module. With
### no droid card it fails - which would be fine, except that its failure path
### is buggy: it aborts the whole daemon on the way out.
###
###   E: module-droid-hidl.c: Couldn't get hw module functions,
###      is module-droid-card loaded?
###   E: protocol-dbus.c: Assertion 'p' failed at
###      ../src/pulsecore/protocol-dbus.c:1116, function
###      pa_dbus_protocol_unregister_extension(). Aborting.
###
### pa_dbus_protocol_unregister_extension() asserts on a NULL protocol object,
### because the module unregisters an extension it never registered. Upstream's
### .nofail wrapper does not help: .nofail only tolerates a module *declining*
### to load, and this one calls abort().
###
### The result was PulseAudio crash-looping with the ALSA sink already created
### and working - "Loaded module-alsa-sink", sink.primary-out INIT -> IDLE,
### default_sink set - and then dying two lines later, so every client got
### "Connection refused".
###
### module-droid-hidl does nothing useful here anyway. Despite the name it no
### longer speaks HIDL; it only forwards set_parameters()/get_parameters() out
### of PulseAudio to the droid hw module, and there is no droid hw module.
### pulseaudio-modules-droid-hidl is also dropped from the adaptation pattern,
### so on a fresh image the .ifexists below would fail anyway. This file keeps
### the daemon safe even if something else pulls the package back in.

### If droid-card needs other arguments than the default, have the new
### load-module line in /etc/pulse/arm_droid_card_custom.pa
.ifexists /etc/pulse/arm_droid_card_custom.pa
 .include /etc/pulse/arm_droid_card_custom.pa
.else
 load-module module-droid-card rate=48000
.endif

### Needed on devices with older Android bases.
### HADK guide explains how to implement this fully
.ifexists module-droid-glue.so
 .nofail
 load-module module-droid-glue
 .fail
.endif

### module-droid-hidl deliberately omitted - see the header above.
